            <ArticleTitle>[Pattern-profile of emergency consultations of children in acute asthmatic crisis].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>123-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="BACKGROUND" NlmCategory="BACKGROUND">Asthma is one of the most frequent illnesses in the pediatric age, the exacerbations account for one of the main consult causes to the emergency services.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To determine the frequency of the consultation demand and the recurrence of patients with acute crisis of asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHOD" NlmCategory="METHODS">A transverse study, performed at the service of pediatric emergencies, included pediatric patients with acute crisis of asthma from January to December, 2000.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">In this study 20.3% of the consultations were due to acute crisis of asthma, 54.29% needed handling in the service of pediatric emergencies with inhalotherapy; 94.3% responded to the treatment. The gender masculine-feminine relationship was of 1.7:1. The predominant ages were from 3 to 5 years. The consultation increased in September, October and November.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">When asthma is mistreated may present exacerbations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
